{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"Alport syndrome is a genetic condition characterized by kidney disease, hearing loss, and eye abnormalities.","source_span":"Alport syndrome is a genetic condition characterized by kidney disease, hearing loss, and eye abnormalities."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"Most affected individuals experience progressive loss of kidney function, usually resulting in end-stage kidney disease.","source_span":"Most affected individuals experience progressive loss of kidney function, usually resulting in end-stage kidney disease."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"People with Alport syndrome frequently develop sensorineural hearing loss in late childhood or early adolescence.","source_span":"People with Alport syndrome also frequently develop sensorineural hearing loss in late childhood or early adolescence."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"The eye abnormalities seen in Alport syndrome seldom lead to vision loss.","source_span":"The eye abnormalities seen in this condition seldom lead to vision loss."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"About 80% of Alport syndrome cases are inherited in an X-linked manner and caused by mutations in the COL4A5 gene.","source_span":"In 80% of cases, Alport syndrome is inherited in an X-linked manner and is caused by mutations in the COL4A5 gene."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"The remaining Alport syndrome cases may be inherited in an autosomal recessive or autosomal dominant manner and are caused by mutations in the COL4A3 or COL4A4 genes.","source_span":"In the remaining cases, it may be inherited in either an autosomal recessive or autosomal dominant manner and caused by mutations in the COL4A3 or COL4A4 genes."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"Treatment for Alport syndrome may include use of a hearing aid, hemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis for end-stage renal failure, and kidney transplantation.","source_span":"Treatment may include use of a hearing aid; hemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis to treat those with end-stage renal failure; and kidney transplantation."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"In males, one altered copy of the COL4A5 gene in each cell is sufficient to cause kidney failure and other severe symptoms of Alport syndrome.","source_span":"In males (who have only one X chromosome), one altered copy of the COL4A5 gene in each cell is sufficient to cause kidney failure and other severe symptoms of the disorder."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"In females, a mutation in only one copy of the COL4A5 gene usually only results in hematuria, though some women experience more severe symptoms.","source_span":"In females (who have two X chromosomes), a mutation in only one copy of the COL4A5 gene usually only results in hematuria, but some women experience more severe symptoms."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"Fathers cannot pass X-linked traits, such as the X-linked form of Alport syndrome, to their sons.","source_span":"A characteristic of X-linked inheritance is that fathers cannot pass X-linked traits to their sons."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"Type IV collagen is an important component of the organ of Corti, an inner ear structure that transforms sound waves into nerve impulses for the brain.","source_span":"Type IV collagen is also an important component of the organ of Corti, an inner ear structure that transforms sound waves into nerve impulses for the brain."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"ACE inhibitors can help reduce proteinuria and the progression of kidney disease in Alport syndrome.","source_span":"Research suggests that ACE inhibitors can help reduce proteinuira and the progression of kidney disease."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"About 10% of Alport syndrome patients who receive a kidney transplant develop nephritis in the graft.","source_span":"some studies have reported that about 10% of transplanted patients develop nephritis in the graft"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"Hearing loss in Alport syndrome is likely to be permanent.","source_span":"Loss of hearing is likely to be permanent."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"Young men with Alport syndrome should use hearing protection in noisy environments.","source_span":"Young men with Alport syndrome should use hearing protection in noisy environments."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d4_0000261","statement":"Glomerulopathy, retinopathy, and sensorineural hearing impairment each occur in approximately 90% of people with Alport syndrome.","source_span":"Glomerulopathy 90% Retinopathy 90% Sensorineural hearing impairment 90%"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000261","fact_refs":[4,5],"question":"What percentage of Alport syndrome cases are caused by X-linked mutations in the COL4A5 gene, and how are the remaining cases inherited?","answer":"About 80% of Alport syndrome cases are inherited in an X-linked manner due to COL4A5 mutations. The remaining cases are inherited in an autosomal recessive or autosomal dominant manner and are caused by mutations in COL4A3 or COL4A4."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000261","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What treatments are used to manage Alport syndrome?","answer":"Treatment may include a hearing aid, hemodialysis or peritoneal dialysis for end-stage renal failure, and kidney transplantation."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000261","fact_refs":[7,8],"question":"Why do males with a COL4A5 mutation tend to have more severe Alport syndrome symptoms than females?","answer":"In males, who have only one X chromosome, a single altered copy of COL4A5 is enough to cause kidney failure and other severe symptoms. In females, who have two X chromosomes, a mutation in only one copy usually causes just hematuria, though some women have more severe symptoms."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000261","fact_refs":[9],"question":"Can a father with the X-linked form of Alport syndrome pass it to his sons?","answer":"No, a characteristic of X-linked inheritance is that fathers cannot pass X-linked traits to their sons."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000261","fact_refs":[12],"question":"What percentage of Alport syndrome patients who undergo kidney transplantation develop nephritis in the transplanted kidney?","answer":"About 10% of transplanted Alport syndrome patients develop nephritis in the graft, though transplantation is usually successful."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000261","fact_refs":[10],"question":"What role does type IV collagen play in the ear structure affected by Alport syndrome?","answer":"Type IV collagen is an important component of the organ of Corti, an inner ear structure that converts sound waves into nerve impulses for the brain."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d4_0000261","fact_refs":[15],"question":"Which three signs occur in about 90% of people with Alport syndrome?","answer":"Glomerulopathy, retinopathy, and sensorineural hearing impairment each occur in approximately 90% of patients with Alport syndrome."}
